      "end": 1.705292,
      "text": "Two contexts. Different beans?"
    },
    {
      "scene": 2,
      "start": 1.785292,
      "end": 8.818042,
      "text": "Yes. Register alpha in context A, and beta in B. Each independent context has its own registry."
    },
    {
      "scene": 3,
      "start": 8.898042,
      "end": 16.071458,
      "text": "Context A finds alpha, but beta is missing. Sharing one Java application doesn't connect these registries."
    },
    {
      "scene": 4,
      "start": 16.151458,
      "end": 22.310583,
      "text": "Create a fresh parent and child. Set the parent before refreshing the child. The registries stay separate."
    },
    {
      "scene": 5,
      "start": 22.390583,
      "end": 27.147417,
      "text": "The child checks locally first. A missing named bean can be found in its parent."
    },
    {
      "scene": 6,
      "start": 27.227417,
      "end": 34.77175,
      "text": "The parent cannot search its children. Our tests confirm both directions: child to parent works; parent to child doesn't."
    },
    {
      "scene": 7,
      "start": 36.77175,
      "end": 37.8625,
      "text": "Thanks for watching."
    }
